// event: completion A Use1.a
// concurrent: completion A Use1.a; completion A Use2.b
// cancel: A
// note: the abort with a waiter (§3.1; abort_waiter_takes_over in the model): reader A is cancelled at each of its safepoints, at every pair; whatever A was completing is released unpublished, and B, waiting on it or arriving later, completes it itself and answers as the sequential run. Under a file root whose reading sentinel is cleared only on publication (dotc's readIndexedDef) the waiter meets the sentinel instead and reports a false cycle
// file: A
class Int {}
class String {}
object Lib { def v = M.m.i; def w = v }
object M { def m = N }
object N { def i: Int; def s: String }
class Use1 { def a = Lib.v; def c = Lib.w }
class Use2 { def b = Lib.v; def d = M.m.s }
